---
/* ============================================================================
   TuitionOpener — the values-led money statement (benchmark backlog #3)
   ============================================================================
   Exeter's admissions page HEADLINES its money values ("not your ability to
   pay"); ours were buried under a standard table header. This code-owned band
   leads /tuition with the transparency moat in display type, above the table.
   Injected by the moments map; copy is evergreen and code-owned (a designed
   artifact like the rating slip, not volunteer content).
   ============================================================================ */
---

<section class="bg-cream" aria-labelledby="tuition-opener-title">
  <div class="wcp-container py-[var(--wcp-space-xl)] text-center">
    <h2
      id="tuition-opener-title"
      class="mx-auto max-w-4xl text-[length:var(--text-h1)] text-balance text-navy"
      data-reveal
    >
      Every fee, published. On purpose.
    </h2>
    <p
      class="mx-auto mt-5 max-w-2xl text-xl leading-relaxed text-ink sm:text-2xl"
      data-reveal
      style="--reveal-delay: 120ms"
    >
      Most preschools make you ask. Ours are all on this page, every dollar, because that is how a
      parent-run co-op treats parents.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
